Say something, please!

256
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,017
I have to know where they're taking me!

257
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:51,000
What are they going to do? Reimi!

258
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:52,930
Dunno.

259
00:13:53,013 --> 00:13:56,111
Although, I doubt we'll be
living in peace and tranquility.

260
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:22,500
Now, at long last, we can
finally pass on, together.

261
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:33,530
What?

262
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:35,740
Are you really leaving us, Reimi?

263
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:40,157
Surely it wouldn't hurt anything if
you stayed a little while longer.

264
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,297
I mean, you've been like a
guardian angel to this town.

265
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,357
I can't imagine life here without you.

266
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,760
Please, you have to stay. Koichi,

267
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:48,997
you're very sweet,

268
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,417
but Arnold and I have done everything
we set out to accomplish here.

269
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,800
The time's come for us to leave Mariah.

270
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:56,572
That's how it has to be.

271
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,780
So, little Rohan,

272
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:02,697
do you think you're going to cry after
we've gone off to the great beyond?

273
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:03,940
In your dreams?

274
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,157
What reason would I have to miss you?

275
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:09,240
You died 15 years ago,
making you a distant memory.

276
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:12,997
I've said this before, but
spirits should really just let go.

277
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:15,677
Haunting the world of the
living is so out of style.

278
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,997
A soul's final resting
place isn't here with us,

279
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,315
but exploring the uncharted afterlife.

280
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:32,517
Fine, I'll say it, alright, but I'm only
doing so because I'll never see you again.

281
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,480
I'll miss you.

282
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,760
Of course I don't want you to go.

283
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,310
Yo.

284
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:44,540
Hey, you're all here.

285
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:47,500
So it's all over, Reimi?

286
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:49,090
Oh, wow.

287
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,997
Looks like everyone showed up.

288
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,845
We've all come to say goodbye.

289
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:57,140
You guys.

290
00:15:57,820 --> 00:16:00,761
It feels weird to say this
to the dearly departed.

291
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,037
But take care of yourself.

292
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,944
See you on the other side, Kay.

293
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:07,560
You're an extraordinary young woman, dear.

294
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:17,862
Oh, Reimi, thank you so
much for all you've done.

295
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:20,957
You saved this little town when
it needed a savior the most.

296
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,040
Thank you for saying that, Koichi.

297
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:26,137
But we saved Mariah, all of us together.

298
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:32,320
As long as we draw breath, no one here
today will ever forget you or your bravery.

299
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,600
Thank you all.

300
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,115
That means the world.

301
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,357
So long, my friends.

302
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,270
Be well.

303
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,120
So long, Reimi. Godspeed.

304
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,400
Rest easy.

305
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,260
Where is he?

306
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,500
It's so late.

307
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,005
I guess he's working overtime.

308
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,887
It would have been nice
if he called, though.

309
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:10,220
Oh, Hayato, you haven't touched your food.

310
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,977
Hurry up before it gets cold.

311
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:15,236
If you're waiting for me,
I'll eat when Dad gets home.

312
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,040
Uh, Hayato?

313
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:21,820
It's okay, Mom.

314
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,198
I'll wait with you.

315
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,200
When dad gets home,

316
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:30,008
we'll all sit down and eat together,
because that's what a family does, right?

317
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:31,870
Sure.

318
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:36,600
Say, am I imagining things, or
have you gotten taller lately?

319
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:42,811
When all was said and done, our little
Morioh wasn't the town it used to be.

320
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,917
A monster named Yoshikage
Kira swept in like

321
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,765
a plague and had his way
with our beloved home.

322
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:53,277
Hayato's mother will no doubt wait
for her husband until the end of time.

323
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:56,077
And Shigechi's parents will never stop

324
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:58,897
waiting for their special
little man to return.

325
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:01,977
Whether a son, daughter,
brother, or sister.

326
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:05,920
Kira's victims belong to parents
who will never give up hope.

327
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:10,340
And yet, that hope will only
cause their pain to grow deeper?

328
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:14,480
The question is, what can
we do to lessen this burden?

329
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:18,057
Will a vile past consume our future,

330
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:21,258
or will we be able to forge
ahead unfettered by fear?

331
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,980
I wish I could say.

332
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:26,140
How about it, Jotaro?

333
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:30,417
You worried about what might
happen when we leave this place?

334
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,120
I am, just a bit.

335
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,737
Because of all of this,

336
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:37,537
we've had the chance to see how
capable Josuke and his friends are.

337
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,914
And there's one thing I can
say with absolute certainty.

338
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:45,057
The young people living in this
town are heroes one and all,

339
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:47,897
and each one of them
possesses a heart of gold.

340
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:51,277
They've the same righteous hearts we
witnessed on our journey to Egypt.

341
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:56,066
They carry a spirit of radiance that will
fight for true justice above all else.

342
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:59,200
I see it in Josuke, as well as the others.

343
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:02,302
Morio's in good hands with them.

344
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:06,457
As long as they're here, we
have nothing to worry about.

345
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,820
Hey, old man!

346
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,877
Don't just stand there gawking!

347
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,440
Answer me! Well,

348
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,917
then guess it's time for
me to say goodbye to a

349
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,200
great son who's made his
father so very proud Hey,

350
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:18,797
remember that picture of mom.

351
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,057
I gave you a while ago.

352
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:21,417
You don't still have it.

353
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:22,330
Do you?

354
00:19:22,413 --> 00:19:25,017
Course I do I put it in my
wallet for safe keeping just

355
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:28,157
like you told me to ah since
I can't tell her in person.

356
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:31,534
I'll tell you I wish her all
the happiness in the world.

357
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,860
So funny thing about that picture.

358
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:38,080
I gave you I decided to hang on to a piece

359
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,000
Shining Diamond

360
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,317
Oh wow, you shouldn't have.

361
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,297
Though I'll take it if you insist.

362
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:51,417
We'll just call this gift
16 years of back allowance.

363
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:54,137
Besides, think about what
your better half would say.

364
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:55,337
If you took that picture over you?

365
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:57,596
Who does that cocky punk think he is?

366
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,257
I'm starting to see that
golden spirit, old man.

367
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,920
And he's seeing it all
the way to the bank!

368
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:05,880
You take good care of yourself. Help!

369
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:14,168
The invisible baby's
mother was never found.

370
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:18,771
So, Joseph Joestar rose to the occasion
and began an adventure as a new dad.

371
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:22,157
Jotaro Kujo finally
finished a doctoral thesis.

372
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:24,257
He began on a species
of starfish he found.

373
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:27,080
on a beach in Mariah, earning him his PhD.

374
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,600
Damn that Josuke!

375
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:34,177
He's always coming in here and eating
all my food like he owns the place!

376
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:35,090
Agh!

377
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:37,060
I'll just drink his juice.

378
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:39,090
Koichi!

379
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:40,390
Huh?

380
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:41,690
Sorry I'm late.

381
00:20:41,773 --> 00:20:45,151
I was making Bind boxes for
us and lost track of the time.

382
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,960
Wow, you actually made us a special lunch?

383
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,355
That's so thoughtful.

384
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,381
Lunchtime can't come soon enough.

385
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:02,410
Tasty!

386
00:21:08,060 --> 00:21:10,472
Now we're cookin', let the healing begin!

387
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:13,014
Don't fight it, let the food carry you!

388
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:17,020
If this works, you'll be a normal
old dad again, isn't that great?

389
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:23,180
Well, that didn't work.

390
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,020
My skin is so smooth!

391
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:30,417
Check out my refreshed eyes, the
food hair is out of this world!

392
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,330
Isn't it though?

393
00:21:31,413 --> 00:21:34,631
Thanks to this food, I'm even
more stunningly gorgeous now.

394
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,017
What am I gonna do with myself?

395
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,337
You're simply radiant, you!

396
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:38,917
Yeah, you're practically beaming.

397
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,240
Mmm, you think so?

398
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:43,755
Would you say I'm a dazzling
dish of devilish delights?

399
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:49,560
Well, amigo mio, until next we meet.

400
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:55,160
I just saw Ko holding hands with a girl,
and she was drop-dead gorgeous. Oh, my!

401
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:58,697
Are you sure he never mentioned
anything to me about a girlfriend?

402
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:02,240
Did you hear? Mr. Kira
went missing. Yeah, I did.

403
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:06,360
They're saying they found him
dead without a face. How freaky.

404
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,557
And just how are you going
to make this up to me?

405
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,470
Say what?

406
00:22:09,553 --> 00:22:13,117
That stupid can you kicked Spray
Juice all over my brand new manga.

407
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,277
So I want to know what you're
going to do to make this right.

408
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,889
Jeez, kid, cry me a river.

409
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:25,100
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

410
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:27,700
All right, let's get started.

411
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:43,537
You sure spend a lot of time
staring out into the distance.

412
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:44,777
You see anything cool?

413
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:47,140
I just see plain old Morioh.

414
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:49,680
Exactly, isn't it grand?

415
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,560
I find this town interesting,
quite interesting indeed.

416
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:59,200
And so, for most, the summer of
1999 slipped away like any other.

417
00:22:59,460 --> 00:23:03,420
Peace had come to Morioh, making
for some pretty great days.

418
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,800
Hey, did you hear?

419
00:23:09,380 --> 00:23:10,210
Hmm?

420
00:23:10,293 --> 00:23:13,197
Apparently, Rohan got caught
shoplifting from Kamehuu.

421
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,340
What a dim shit.

422
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:15,710
Huh?

423
00:23:15,793 --> 00:23:17,832
Man, that's freaking crazy, if it's true.

424
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,137
What do you mean by it?

425
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:20,480
I mean it has to be.

426
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,365
Wait, you don't know for sure?

427
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,950
Dumbass.

428
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:26,000
Well, come on, let's bounce.
